{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Finishing up: Visualizing Datatypes - Tabular data with Pandas\n",
    "1. Tabular data\n",
    "   1. with Pandas (https://pandas.pydata.org/)\n",
    "   1. ~~with NumPy (https://numpy.org/) (probably not time though... maybe next time?)~~\n",
    "\n",
    "### and \n",
    "\n",
    "# Colormaps\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "**NOTE:** we will probably not cover all of the material listed here, but its included as extra materials for fun!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's start this notebook by importing our usual things:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#%matplotlib inline\n",
    "import matplotlib\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "#matplotlib.rcParams[\"font.family\"] = \"sans-serif\" # note, could also use like \"sans-serif\" others, just google\n",
    "\n",
    "# lets also import numpy\n",
    "import numpy as np"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 1. Tabular Data with Pandas"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Let's also try making some histograms from tabular data, in this case a CSV file.\n",
    "\n",
    "Make sure you have the building inventory downloaded from the class website! https://uiuc-ischool-dataviz.github.io/is445_AOUAOG_fall2021/week02/data/building_inventory.csv\n",
    "\n",
    "You can also learn more about this dataset on its original site: https://data.illinois.gov/dataset/87building_inventory"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can also do a lot of these things with the `pandas` library.\n",
    "\n",
    "(This is something you can pip or anaconda install if you need to.)\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll import pandas with the \"pd\" shorthand to make our lives easier:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# You can download a CSV file and read from where you've downloaded:\n",
    "#buildings = pd.read_csv('/Users/jillnaiman/Downloads/building_inventory.csv')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Note: you can read directly from the web: "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "buildings = pd.read_csv('https://uiuc-ischool-dataviz.github.io/is445_spring2022/week03/data/building_inventory.csv')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
